1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,550
Synthetic control and synthetic DiD — Build a comparison unit that tracks the treated one

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:09,450
One treated unit and a pool of potential controls. Their simple average (dashed) does not follow the treated unit before treatment.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:17,950
Synthetic control chooses weights on control units so that their weighted average tracks the treated unit before treatment (Abadie et al. 2010).

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,950
After treatment, the gap between the treated unit and its synthetic twin is the estimated effect.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,950
Synthetic DiD (Arkhangelsky et al. 2021) also weights the pre-treatment years and allows a level shift, so it only has to match trends, not levels.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,950
Useful with few treated units when no comparison group has parallel trends on its own. Stata: sdid, synth.
